{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_doc": "Baseline cases for the covmar migration. Each case fixes the real data and model exactly. levels_run: 'engine' = frozen arrays straight into the fitter; 'model' = built through data container -> contrast -> spec -> fit. Diagonal / block-diagonal V cases are engine-only because the phd model layer cannot express them; bootstrap cases are model-only because the bootstrap lives in the model layer. factors map canonical level names to dataset columns. correlated lists the multivariate levels with a full 2x2 covariance (null for univariate). V: 'dense' full sampling covariance; 'diag' its diagonal only; 'blockdiag' within-outcome covariance kept, between-outcome sampling covariance zeroed. Covariates enter X untransformed (no centring), as in the phd code.",
